{
  "id": "p18",
  "title": "Text Files",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p18-l1",
      "title": "assign and rewrite",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A text file variable has the type text. assign(f, 'NOTES.TXT') connects it to a file name, rewrite(f) creates the file (empty), and writeln(f, …) writes into it, just like on the screen.",
        "close(f) finishes the file. Without it, the last lines might never reach the disk.",
        "The lessons run on a small simulated floppy disk. Files you write stay there until the program ends."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Write;",
          "var",
          "  f: text;",
          "begin",
          "  assign(f, 'NOTES.TXT');",
          "  rewrite(f);",
          "  writeln(f, 'Turbo Pascal notes');",
          "  writeln(f, 'Version ', 3);",
          "  close(f);",
          "  writeln('Saved NOTES.TXT');",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "Saved NOTES.TXT"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p18-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does rewrite(f) do?",
          "options": [
            "Creates the file, empty",
            "Reads the file",
            "Deletes the program",
            "Adds to the end of the file"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "An existing file with that name is overwritten."
        },
        {
          "id": "p18-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What connects f with a file name?",
          "options": [
            "assign(f, 'NAME.TXT')",
            "open(f)",
            "f := 'NAME.TXT'",
            "file(f)"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "assign comes first."
        },
        {
          "id": "p18-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Write the score into the file.",
          "code": [
            "  writeln(___, 'Score: ', score);"
          ],
          "options": [
            "f",
            "text",
            "file",
            "'NOTES.TXT'"
          ],
          "answer": "f",
          "explanation": "The file variable comes first in write and writeln."
        },
        {
          "id": "p18-l1-e4",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the lines in order.",
          "lines": [
            "assign(f, 'LOG.TXT');",
            "rewrite(f);",
            "writeln(f, 'started');",
            "close(f);"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "assign(f, 'LOG.TXT');",
            "rewrite(f);",
            "writeln(f, 'started');",
            "close(f);"
          ],
          "explanation": "assign, rewrite, write, close."
        },
        {
          "id": "p18-l1-e5",
          "type": "find_bug",
          "prompt": "This program stops with Runtime error 103: File not open. Which line is missing?",
          "code": [
            "program Log;",
            "var",
            "  f: text;",
            "begin",
            "  assign(f, 'LOG.TXT');",
            "  writeln(f, 'hello');",
            "  close(f);",
            "end."
          ],
          "answer": 5,
          "explanation": "The file must be opened first: rewrite(f); between assign and writeln."
        },
        {
          "id": "p18-l1-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why call close(f)?",
          "options": [
            "So everything really reaches the disk",
            "To delete the file",
            "To read it",
            "It's not needed"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Writing is buffered; close finishes it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p18-l2",
      "title": "reset and readln",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "To read a file, assign it and call reset(f). Then readln(f, s) reads one line into s, and readln(f, n) a number.",
        "If the file doesn't exist, reset stops the program with Runtime error 2: File not found.",
        "This disk already has a file SCORES.TXT with three lines like ADA 92."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Read;",
          "var",
          "  f: text;",
          "  line: string;",
          "begin",
          "  assign(f, 'SCORES.TXT');",
          "  reset(f);",
          "  readln(f, line);",
          "  writeln('First line: ', line);",
          "  readln(f, line);",
          "  writeln('Second line: ', line);",
          "  close(f);",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": [
          "First line: ADA 92",
          "Second line: KEN 78"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "p18-l2-e1",
